  "presentation_summary": [
    "41-year-old gravida 5 para 4 woman at 34 weeks with dichorionic-diamniotic twin gestation presented for the second time to the ED.",
    "Symptoms were severe epigastric and right upper quadrant pain associated with middle back pain and nausea.",
    "She had known choledocholithiasis, tobacco use, and class III obesity.",
    "Exam showed marked epigastric and right upper quadrant tenderness.",
    "Labs at 34 weeks showed WBC 12.1 x10^9/L, ALP 160 U/L, AST 16 U/L, ALT 9 U/L, total bilirubin 0.5 mg/dL, and albumin 3.2 g/dL.",
    "RUQ ultrasound showed a distended gallbladder containing nonmobile gallstones and sludge impacted in the gallbladder neck, normal wall thickness, positive sonographic Murphy sign, CBD 5 mm, normal pancreas, and splenomegaly."
  ],
